     "body": "<p>As of 539a62ad3ce72d68d4f9d37a9d481d1455658a3a on master, fcrepo with Eclipse is pretty close to where it was at for me prior to m2e 0.13.</p>\n\n<p>For posterity, here are the install steps I used:</p>\n\n<p>Download Eclipse Indigo (3.7.1)<br/>\n\t<a href=\"http://www.eclipse.org/downloads/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.eclipse.org/downloads/</a><br/>\n\tSelect \"Eclipse IDE for Java EE Developers\" Mac OS X 64 Bit</p>\n\n<p>Install m2e<br/>\n\tOpen Eclipse Marketplace<br/>\n\tsearch for \"m2e\"<br/>\n\tselect \"Maven Integration for Eclipse\" for installation<br/>\n\tConfirm installation (version 1.0.100.20110804-1717)<br/>\n\t\tm2e - Maven Integration for Eclipse<br/>\n\t\tm2e - slf4j over logback logging</p>\n\n<p>\tOpen Eclipse Marketplace<br/>\n\tsearch for \"m2e\"<br/>\n\tSelect \"Maven Integration for Eclipse WTP\" for installation</p>\n\n<p>Install EGit<br/>\n\tsearch for \"git\"<br/>\n\tSelect \"EGit - Git Team Provider\" for installation<br/>\n\tConfirm installation<br/>\n\t\tEclipse EGit<br/>\n\t\tEclipse JGit</p>",
     "created": "13/Jan/12 12:08 PM",
